      "panel-6": {
        "kind": "Panel",
        "spec": {
          "data": {
            "kind": "QueryGroup",
            "spec": {
              "queries": [
                {
                  "kind": "PanelQuery",
                  "spec": {
                    "hidden": false,
                    "query": {
                      "datasource": {
                        "name": "loki"
                      },
                      "group": "loki",
                      "kind": "DataQuery",
                      "spec": {
                        "direction": "backward",
                        "editorMode": "code",
                        "expr": "avg_over_time({service=\"cardano-node/leios-voting\", instance=~\"$instance\", kind=\"LeiosEbValidated\"} | json | label_format hit=`{{ divf .reapplied (addf .reapplied .applied) }}` | unwrap hit [${window}s]) by (instance)",
                        "legendFormat": "{{instance}}",
                        "queryType": "range"
                      },
                      "version": "v0"
                    },
                    "refId": "A"
                  }
                }
              ],
              "queryOptions": {},
              "transformations": []
            }
          },
          "description": "Cache hit rate when the voting thread validates an EB's closure to decide whether to vote for it -- not the apply path that runs when a certified EB's closure is applied to the chain. Of the txs in the closure, the share the LeiosTxCache spared full validation: reapplied means the cache had already validated the tx, so only the state-dependent checks re-ran; applied means it was validated from scratch. Plotted as reapplied / (reapplied + applied).\n\nThe ratio is computed per validation and then averaged over the Rate / avg window, so every validation in the window contributes equally whatever its closure size. Narrow the window to see individual validations; widen it to see the trend. 0 and 1 are common and real: a closure is often entirely cached or entirely fresh.\n\nPer node, since nodes do not see the same announcement at the same time and a fleet aggregate would average over different EB sets. Narrow with the instance variable, or click a legend entry to isolate a node.\n\nA high hit rate does not imply cheap validation -- reapplyTx runs per tx either way, so validation cost tracks closure size, not this ratio. This is also the work that sits inside the vote window, so it is the cost that can make a vote too late.\n\nGaps are windows in which that node validated nothing.\n\nThe panel below measures the same thing weighted by transaction instead of by validation, from counters rather than a log scan. The two answer different questions and are shown together deliberately.",
          "id": 6,
          "links": [],
          "title": "Cache hit rate for voting EB validation, per node",
          "vizConfig": {
            "group": "timeseries",
            "kind": "VizConfig",
            "spec": {
              "fieldConfig": {
                "defaults": {
                  "color": {
                    "mode": "palette-classic"
                  },
                  "custom": {
